# 017 · Remove the legacy model names

**Status:** `VERIFIED` · **Version:** [v0.1.0](../roadmap.md#v010) · **Part:** Install from images

## What

Remove the old `QWEN_*` aliases of the model settings, the `thermite-qwen` provider ID and the `qwen-api-key` file migration. Change the Kubernetes namespace default from `ar-{rig}` to `thermite-{rig}`.

## Why

They are names from Thermite's first deployment, and they confuse new users.

## Done when

- [x] No old name is read or documented.
- [x] A deployment that sets its namespace explicitly sees no change.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-18, owner: Remove them after the maintainers' own deployment switches to the new names.

## Open questions

None.

## Progress

- 2026-10-19: Goal written from the v0.1.0 release plan.
- 2026-10-19: The namespace default can change now, because the maintainers' deployment sets its namespace explicitly. The model-name aliases wait until that deployment stops using them.
- 2026-10-20: Done, at the release lead's request. The harness reads the model route only from `THERMITE_MODEL_*` and `THERMITE_AGENT_HARNESS`; the broker and `thermite selftest isolation` no longer read `QWEN_API_KEY_FILE`. An OpenAI-compatible route registers as `thermite-openai`. `npm run dev:init` writes `model-api-key` only, and no longer copies an older key file. The `kubernetes` lifecycle driver names each rig's namespace `thermite-{rig}` when `THERMITE_K8S_NAMESPACE` is not set or is empty. A set template is kept, and so are the namespaces control stores for the rigs it sets up on clusters. The settings and command-line references say so, and the docs check fails on a page that names a `QWEN_` setting. Tests: `src/harness/agents/planner.test.ts` (the old names make no route; the provider ID) and `src/control/lifecycle.test.ts` (the default, an empty value and a set template).
- 2026-10-20: What an existing deployment changes. Nothing that control or a rig stores holds the old names: the provider ID lived only in memory, and control keeps each cluster's namespace pattern and each cluster rig's namespace. A deployment that still sets a `QWEN_` model setting sets the `THERMITE_MODEL_*` name instead (`QWEN_API_KEY_FILE` becomes `THERMITE_MODEL_API_KEY_FILE`). A local checkout with only `.dev/secrets/qwen-api-key` renames it to `model-api-key`. A control with `THERMITE_LIFECYCLE=kubernetes` and no `THERMITE_K8S_NAMESPACE`, whose rigs are in `ar-` namespaces, sets `THERMITE_K8S_NAMESPACE=ar-{rig}`.

